.\" man/man5/docv-config.5
.TH DOCV\-CONFIG 5 2026-11-03 "docv 0.1.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
docv\-config \- configuration file of docv
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/docv/config.ini
.SH DESCRIPTION
The configuration of
.MR docv 1
is an INI file in
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/docv/config.ini ,
or
.I ~/.config/docv/config.ini
when
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset or not an absolute path.
The first run writes it with every setting at its default, most of them
commented out.
.PP
A line
.BI [ section ]
starts a section; a line
.IB key " = " value
sets a key in it.
Lines starting with
.B ;
or
.B #
are comments; a comment cannot follow a value on the same line.
An unknown section or key, or an invalid value, is an error:
.B docv
reports it and exits with status 1.
.SH "THE [roff] SECTION"
.TP
.B unsafe
Run the roff requests that execute commands or access files, and the
.B \eV
escape (environment variables).
Default
.BR false .
Booleans are
.BR true / false ,
.BR yes / no ,
.BR on / off
or
.BR 1 / 0 ,
in any case.
.RS
.PP
With
.BR true :
.B sy
and
.B pso
run commands with
.IR /bin/sh ,
.B pso
reading the output as input;
.B pi
pipes the page, formatted as text at 78 columns, into a command after
parsing;
.BR open ,
.BR opena ,
.BR write ,
.BR writec ,
.B writem
and
.B close
write files;
.B cf
and
.B trf
copy files into the page;
.B rd
reads input lines from the terminal, for the page named on the command line
only.
Commands run with standard input and output on the null device.
.PP
With
.B false
these requests are accepted and ignored.
Manual pages are input from third parties: enable this only if you trust
every page you open.
.RE
.SH "THE [viewer] SECTION"
.TP
.B start\-wrapped
Start in the wrapped layout, paragraphs filled to the width of the
terminal.
With
.BR false ,
the viewer starts in the unwrapped layout: one line per paragraph, scrolled
sideways.
Default
.BR true .
.B w
switches between the layouts, and
.B \-u
on the command line starts unwrapped either way.
.SH "THE [colors] SECTION"
Every element of the viewer is drawn in a role, and each key of this
section restyles one role.
A style is a list of words: attributes
.RB ( bold ,
.BR italic ,
.BR underline ,
.BR reverse ,
.BR dim ),
a foreground color, and
.B on
followed by a background color.
.PP
A color is
.BR default ,
.BR foreground ,
.BR background ,
one of the ANSI colors
.BR black ,
.BR red ,
.BR green ,
.BR yellow ,
.BR blue ,
.BR magenta ,
.BR cyan ,
.BR white ,
each also with a
.B bright\-
prefix, a palette number
.B 0
to
.BR 255 ,
or
.BI # rrggbb\c
\&.
Named and numbered colors are those of the terminal's theme.
A suffix
.BI + n
or
.BI \- n
ramps a color
.I n
percent toward the theme's foreground or background:
.B on background+12
is a background a shade off the terminal's in a dark and a light theme
alike, and
.B foreground\-40
is text dimmed toward the background.
.PP
With
.B NO_COLOR
set, colors are off and this section is ignored; the roles use attributes
only.
.PP
The roles and their defaults:
.TP
.B text
(plain) Plain page text.
.TP
.B heading1
.RB ( "bold bright\-blue" )
Section headings of manual pages, level 1 headings of documents.
.TP
.B heading2
.RB ( "bold blue" )
Subsection headings of manual pages, level 2 headings of documents.
.TP
.B heading3
.RB ( "bold bright\-magenta" )
Level 3 headings.
.TP
.B heading4
.RB ( "bold magenta" )
Level 4 headings.
.TP
.B heading5
.RB ( bold )
Level 5 headings.
.TP
.B heading6
.RB ( "bold foreground\-40" )
Level 6 headings.
.TP
.B bold
.RB ( "bold cyan" )
Bold page text: commands, options.
.TP
.B italic
.RB ( "underline green" )
Italic page text: arguments.
.TP
.B bold\-italic
.RB ( "bold underline green" )
Bold italic page text.
.TP
.B underline
.RB ( underline )
Underlined page text.
.TP
.B code
.RB ( "yellow on background+8" )
Inline code in documents.
.TP
.B code\-block
.RB ( yellow )
Code blocks in documents.
.TP
.B quote
.RB ( foreground\-60 )
The bars of block quotes.
.TP
.B image
.RB ( "italic foreground\-40" )
The description standing for an image.
.TP
.B link
.RB ( "underline magenta" )
Links: cross-references, files, headings, URLs.
.TP
.B link\-focus
.RB ( "reverse magenta" )
The focused link.
.TP
.B text\-selection
.RB ( "on blue\-50" )
Text selected with the mouse.
.TP
.B page\-header
.RB ( foreground\-40 )
The pinned page header and footer.
.TP
.B title
.RB ( bold )
The title.
.TP
.B version
.RB ( foreground\-50 )
The version after the title.
.TP
.B close
.RB ( red )
The close mark.
.TP
.B border
.RB ( foreground\-60 )
The line under the title row, the horizontal scrollbar track and box edges.
.TP
.B thumb
.RB ( "bold blue" )
Scrollbar thumbs.
.TP
.B rule
.RB ( foreground\-70 )
The rules under the page header and above the page footer, and horizontal
rules in documents.
.TP
.B field
.RB ( "on background+12" )
The search bar; its ends take its background as their color.
.TP
.B prompt
.RB ( "bold blue" )
The leading
.B /
of a page search.
.TP
.B placeholder
.RB ( foreground\-50 )
The hint in the empty search bar.
.TP
.B cursor
.RB ( reverse )
The cursor of the search bar.
.TP
.B message
.RB ( yellow )
Messages in the status row.
.TP
.B status
.RB ( foreground\-30 )
The status row.
.TP
.B status\-separator
.RB ( foreground\-60 )
The separators between status parts.
.TP
.B name
.RB ( "bold cyan" )
Page and document names in the page list, and keys in the help.
.TP
.B detail
.RB ( foreground\-35 )
Page and document descriptions in the page list.
.TP
.B selection
.RB ( "on background+22" )
The selected page in the list; the line of the selected match in the page.
.TP
.B hover
.RB ( "on background+10" )
The listed page under the pointer.
.TP
.B mark
.RB ( "bold underline yellow" )
Characters matched by a search.
.TP
.B popup
.RB ( "on background+6" )
The help box.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
[roff]
unsafe = false

[viewer]
start\-wrapped = false

[colors]
heading1 = bold #ff8800
field = on background+8
selection = black on bright\-cyan
link = underline 208
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.MR docv 1
